From 3c624f4f9f6b4566497ca49e8cbd90accfeabaf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:01:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a supported reopen after success reaches
 normal dispatch (recent_success/active_pr)

`hermes kanban reopen` (reopen_done_task) emits `reopened`, which the respawn guard's
recent_success step did not count as a deliberate re-run (only status/promoted/unblocked/
reclaimed), so a card reopened right after completing sat held for the 1 h window.

- reopened_after(): a `reopened` event with the supported payload (previous_status=done)
  STRICTLY after the latest completed run lifts recent_success; same-second/older/malformed
  reopens and unrelated events stay guarded. One reopen authorizes one rerun: the rerun's
  own completion is newer and guards again.
- active_pr: the same strict reopen after the newest PR comment lets the PR owner resume
  THAT PR once; its next PR comment guards again.
- reopen_done_task writes its REOPENED note through add_comment (nested) so it carries
  `commented` provenance (chat/FYI). Before, a reason naming the PR was an unmatched,
  owned publication candidate in the same second as the reopen, holding it active_pr.

- reopened_after and the moved is_handoff_event live in kanban_db_dispatch_rerun.py
  (kanban_db_dispatch.py file cap).

RED: the new dispatch tests fail on main with respawn_guarded == [(tid, 'recent_success')].
Mutants (strict tie, payload check, active_pr lift, add_comment provenance, recent_success
lift): 5/5 killed.

Why-chain: live t_01a19fc2faa99ef8 run 29063 completed 1793685957; reopened 1793686975;
respawn_guarded recent_success 1793686978. Existing reopen tests asserted status only,
never dispatch. Recurrence of t_e67c8a57 (t_7ba3127e), closed without a core change.
Replay over hub kanban.db + boards + sync-shadow: 3 real reopened events, 1 changes
(t_01a19fc2faa99ef8 recent_success -> released); 1 legacy {"by":"supervisor"} event stays guarded.
